death stranding is finally here from the  beginning Hideo Kojima's latest game has  been shrouded in mystery from a baby  giving us a thumbs up to Norman Reedus  his entire ass  the initial trailers left us confused  but wanting more  there's no denying yet death stranding  is a trippy game to celebrate its  release we've come up with a list of the  five trickiest games to enjoy after  you've gotten a taste of the strange  unconventional game that is death  stranding Metal Gear Solid 2 Sons of  Liberty at first Metal Gear Solid 2 just  seemed like a quality sequel to 1998  Metal Gear Solid there were familiar  faces its gameplay and storyline are  similar and Metal Gear still needs to be  stopped but just as you grow comfortable  with your mission and ride in the story  flips on its head after you learn about  the Patriots and their control over  global information your mission goes  from saving the president from dead cell  to destroying a government built AI that  controls the flow of information  information that directly involves you  on your mission the twists and turns  this story pulls you through our Ward  winning and will have you questioning  every action you make and every plot  point in the story by the time you feel  like you know all there is to know the  story throws another curveball  continually making you feel like a pawn  upon completing the game you feel  mentally awakened and broken at the same  time only to be treated by a cliffhanger  post-credit scene they're already dead  all 12 of them when did it happen  about a hundred years ago Bioshock the  story of Bioshock is as memorable as it  is freaky the twisted plot constantly  plays with your expectations giving you  a false sense of control and purpose as  you navigate the underwater city of  Rapture you learn more about its  disturbing past and fall from grace you  discover a city plagued by corruption  genetic mutation and a warped philosophy  and with no contact from the surface  world your only encounters are with the  terrifying inhabitants of Rapture  splicers big daddies and little sisters  these genetically altered beings are the  products of a disturbing series of  events that unfolds and grows all the  more intriguing the further  progress which ultimately leads to one  of the most shocking endings in modern  videogames eternal darkness sanity's  requiem in 2002 the Nintendo GameCube  was gifted a strange little exclusive  that bent the rules of survival horror  by breaking the fourth wall in a number  of unique ways it made you vulnerable  through your playthrough not just from  the unsettling story but from some of  its deceptive in-game mechanics when  encountering enemies the game will trick  you in numerous ways including falsely  ending the game pretending to delete  save files and even blue screen in your  game this can be prevented by keeping  the game sanity meter in check but if it  drops near enemies these disorienting  effects make it hard for you to focus  the on-screen character will start to  audibly panic and the effects will start  to take place even with no enemies  present the entire experience makes you  and the character feel insane and no  longer in control this unique feeling of  helplessness and terror is one that will  always make this game stand out not only  in the GameCubes library but in all  video games amnesia the Dark Descent on  the surface amnesia the Dark Descent may  just seem like a streamer friendly good  time but this indie survival horror game  messes with your head like few others  can your journey begins in a dark castle  where you have no memory of the past  events the darkness surrounding you  quickly becomes your main enemy this  game's plot is fragmented making you  rebuild your memory by way of journal  entries written by your character Daniel  you roam around in the darkness without  a weapon hoping to uncover the truth of  your past quickly before going  completely insane or getting jumpscared  what results is an otherworldly plot  including interdimensional beings  torture and a mysterious mind  controlling orb since the games 2010  launch its impact on indie survival  horror games cannot be ignored  Silent Hill the original Silent Hill  pulls no punches with its delusional  story immediately after the opening  scene you are thrown into a world  created by nightmares as you search for  your daughter in the fog-covered town  you'll meet others along the way only to  end up with more questions than answers  it carries themes of death greed rebirth  and fear alongside many others the  terrifying enemies you face are  manifestations of these themes that  represent the darker side of human  psyche and society as a whole silent  hill's tone and psychological story  carry over into its gameplay it's dark  you always feel lost and you witness  it's disturbing themes come to life if  you want an ordinary survival horror  title look elsewhere because Silent Hill  will mess with your head unlike any  other this was only a handful some of  our favorite trickiest games so in the  comments let us know which are some of  your favorites thanks for watching  you
 

